 "slug": "moon-gone/c01",
 "chapter": "Cold open",
 "topic": "What if the Moon disappeared tonight?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "It's nine forty-seven on a Tuesday night. You're on the roof with your best friend Mo and a borrowed telescope, because your little sister Ellie needs a drawing of the full Moon for school."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "You look down to sharpen your pencil. You look back up. And the Moon is gone."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "Not behind a cloud. Not an eclipse. There's just a round, black hole in the sky where it used to be."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "Down the street, every dog starts barking at once. Every phone in the neighborhood lights up."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "Mo slowly lowers the telescope. 'Okay,' he says. 'Where did it go?'"
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "And by the next morning, the ocean at the end of your street hasn't come back in."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "So what would really happen if the Moon disappeared tonight? The first night, the first year, and a million years from now."
  }
 ],
